<h1>John Michael Allegretti</h1>
<p>Judge up for retention, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Incumbent.</p>
<p>Circuit Court of Cook County</p>
<h2>Ratings</h2>
<ul>
<li>Chicago Bar Association: <a href="https://www.chicagobar.org/votejudges#:~:text=John%20Michael%20Allegretti" rel="nofollow noopener">Qualified</a></li>
<li>Illinois State Bar Association: <a href="https://www.isba.org/judicial-elections/counties/cook#:~:text=John%20Michael%20Allegretti" rel="nofollow noopener">Yes</a></li>
</ul>
<h2>Record</h2>
<p>A Circuit Court judge since 2014, hearing civil cases including consumer debt, personal injury, and contract disputes in the First Municipal District. Injustice Watch reports that in 2012 he was involved in an unsuccessful push to ban alcohol sales in a Galewood precinct, which critics questioned as racially motivated, the Chicago Tribune reported. He disputes that account and says neighborhood concerns about late-night noise and nuisance prompted the effort. A judge stays on the bench with a yes from 60 percent of voters.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Attorney and general counsel at the Cook County Treasurer&#39;s Office (2011-2014), corporate counsel for North American Real Estate Management (2010-2011), and legal director and general counsel at the Cook County Assessor&#39;s Office (2005-2010); earlier a Cook County assistant state&#39;s attorney (1998-2000 and 2001-2005), a hearing officer for the Illinois Property Tax Appeal Board (1996-1998), and an associate at law firms. Law degree from St. Thomas University (1995).</p>
